    "answer": {
      "short": "$-50$.\n\nThere are 50 consecutive pairs, each with value $-1$.",
      "worked": "There are 50 consecutive pairs, each subtracting an even number from the preceding odd number.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=(1-2)+(3-4)+\\cdots+(99-100)\\\\1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=\\underbrace{(-1)+(-1)+\\cdots+(-1)}_{50\\text{ terms}}\\\\1-2+3-4+\\cdots+99-100&=-50.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
